is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Deland.\n\n* WHEN...Until Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 4.0 feet, Docks and piers are completely submerged at\nPier 44 Marina. Many docks are partially submerged at Hontoon\nLanding Marina.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 AM EDT Wednesday the stage was 4.0 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 3.5 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 4.0 feet\nthe next couple days. It will then fall below flood stage late in\nthe week.\n- Flood stage is 4.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued late tonight at 1215 AM EDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 281303"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL THURSDAY EVENING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KMLB.FL.W.0004.000000T0000Z-261030T0000Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-10-29T20:00:00-04:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.32a6624b03ca4bdc3923c468120fbeec7a6da027.001.1,2026-10-27T10:04:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a018ff21889eafe6543a9dc3086e3eeb8943dea8.001.1,2026-10-26T21:41:00-04:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLS"],"NationalWeatherService":["FLW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7500757842e62b9acb60d4e4c73594203c88a316.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-106.15,36.08],[-106.11,36.1],[-106.07,36.06],[-106.1,36.03],[-106.15,36.08]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7500757842e62b9acb60d4e4c73594203c88a316.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7500757842e62b9acb60d4e4c73594203c88a316.001.1","areaDesc":"Rio Arriba, NM","geocode":{"SAME":["035039"],"UGC":["NMC039"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/NMC039"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d80abff4b7e151bb6f7b8c13aff75d770cd9eb6d.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d80abff4b7e151bb6f7b8c13aff75d770cd9eb6d.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-10-27T11:53:00-06:00"}],"sent":"2026-10-27T18:50:00-06:00","effective":"2026-10-27T18:50:00-06:00","onset":"2026-10-27T18:50:00-06:00","expires":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-06:00","ends":null,"status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Albuquerque NM","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 27 at 6:50PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in New\nMexico...\n\nRio Chama Below Chamita affecting Rio Arriba County.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Chama below Chamita.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 6.0 feet, properties in the flood plain along the Rio\nChama and near the junction of the Rio Ojo Caliente will see water\nin their yards. Impacts can include bank erosion and damage to\nwells and septic tanks.  These impacts will increase in severity at\nhigher river levels.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:00 PM MDT Tuesday the stage was 6.4 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 6:00 PM MDT Tuesday was 6.7 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to oscillate around 6.4 to 6.5\nfeet through Wednesday.\n- Flood stage is 6.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 6.4\nfeet on 07/21/2009.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/abq.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Wednesday afternoon at noon MDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSABQ"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS85 KABQ 280050"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KABQ.FL.W.0012.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cfa50f6a669504223baea6cf773706c7874c5ef7.001.1,2026-10-26T22:39:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.39e8506ed8dbae3b2ee3c1ce6cefcc6409afa700.001.1,2026-10-26T11:52:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a95afcfe227f584256cb76078581dda79ebfad8f.001.1,2026-10-26T09:20:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.465e5eee238988cc5c188140de5744b5af99b4fb.001.1,2026-10-26T19:10:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f08c91f0acee371977de089c46578f9af9ef253f.001.1,2026-10-25T19:24:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6809157c7625c7c8299a6b0b582e7722812a02eb.001.1,2026-10-25T08:26:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b81892c86e6f2364cd456f42102fe2e384f4dd10.001.1,2026-10-25T13:20:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f370ba9d84402b34472bc17123a2c52af14dfdf3.001.1,2026-10-25T07:54:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.55a0d1a6b5d267545b412f4507f6bd6d355c2d14.001.1,2026-10-24T19:41:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.46539f06bc13faf3d205e10c0b0931861afdcc31.001.1,2026-10-24T08:39:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn